.ruff_cache/

# uv.lock IS committed. It was ignored, which meant CI checked out a repo with
# no lockfile and `uv sync` resolved fresh from PyPI on every run — so CI never
# once tested the dependency versions the app actually runs. It surfaced as a
# lint failure (a newer ruff with a wider default rule set found 254 problems
# that the locked ruff does not enforce), but the lint was the symptom.
#
# Lockfiles are committed for applications and ignored for libraries. This is
# an application.

# user health data + local databases — NEVER commit (P1)
data/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite*

.DS_Store

docs/vital-review-teachings.md

# live-eval output: a run artefact, not a source file
crisis-live-eval.txt
Dockerfile.backup

# VAPID keypair from `vapid --gen`. private_key.pem is a signing key: it
# lands in this directory by default and is one `git add -A` from being
# published. The real copy belongs in Secret Manager.
*.pem
